	Ø "sed" command
	- Replaces a string in a file with a new string
	- Find and delete a line
	- Remove empty lines
	- Remove the first or n lines in a file
	- To replace tabs with spaces
	- Show defined lines from a file
	- Substitute within vi editor
	- …..
	
	$ sed 's/oldword/newword/g' filename
	# it doesn’t change in the file just in display console
	$ sed -i 's/oldword/newword/g' filename
	# it will change in file 
	
	$ sed 's/oldword//g' filename
	# deleted the word in the screen
	
	$ sed '/word/d' filename
	# deleted the lines which has the word
	
	$ sed -i '/^$/d' filename
	# deletes the empty lines 
	
	$ sed '1d' filename
	# deleted first line
	
	$ sed '1,2d' filename
	# delete first two lines
	
	$ sed 's/\t/ /g' filename
	# removes tabs
	
	$ sed -n 12,18p filename
	#dispaly 12-18 lines
	
	$ sed 12,18d filename
	# displays everything except 12-18
	
	$ sed G filename
	# every line has an empty line
	
	$ sed '8!s/oldword/Newword/' filename
	# replace word with new word except 8th line
	
	$ vi filename
	:%s/oldword/newword/
	# replaces old word to new word in vi file

